# Public starter rules
#
# The public setup kit deliberately installs no pre-approved command prefixes.
# Codex can create user-level rules when you review and accept an approval
# suggestion in the TUI. You can also add narrowly scoped prefix_rule entries
# here after testing them with:
#
#   codex execpolicy check --pretty --rules "$HOME/.codex/rules/default.rules" -- <command>
#
# Keep machine-specific paths, hostnames, account identifiers, and credentials
# out of reusable rule files.
